{
  "id": "portal-sources",
  "title": "A world seen through a portal, and the world a seat crosses into, shows its own cabinet, its own text and its own camera on its screens",
  "binding": "Both legs boot an offscreen 256x144 lobby whose arch shows the gallery as a window and carries a seat into it, the gallery's arrival arch facing it so the pair maps as the identity. The positive gallery has three screens ten units past its arrival: two lines of text in its own font, its own cabinet's picture in the middle, and a view through its own camera of a green lamp behind the arrival, which no seat looking along the walk sees. world.nesting names the window level's machine source, text and its camera view session$24$camera$lamp, and after the seat crosses, the routed level presenting the gallery names the same sources with its own camera view. Each capture reads one region per screen, by mean code on both backends alike. Through the window: the text region reads 0.17 and is held at least 0.11, the cabinet's lit half 1.0 held at least 0.5, and the camera screen green 0.68 held at least 0.4 with red at most 0.15 and blue at most 0.4. After the crossing: text 0.14, cabinet 1.0 and camera green 0.88 under the same bounds. The discriminating leg boots the same rooms with the gallery's three screens showing nothing: every level lists them as none, each region reads at most 0.08, and every source observation turns red.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": [
    "vulkan",
    "directx"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "gpu"
  ],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
  "fixtures": [
